===Noun===
{{en-noun|p}}

# The [[internal]] [[organ]]s of a human or animal; ''especially'' [[viscera]], [[intestine]]s.
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1970|lyricist=Geezer Butler|artist=w:Black Sabbath|title=Walpurgis (older version of {{w|War Pigs}})|album=Paranoid|text=It's the place for all black sinners. / Watch them eating dead rat's '''innards'''.}}
# The [[inner]] [[working]]s of something; the [[insides]] or [[guts]].
#: {{ux|en|He took the cover off his computer and looked at the '''innards'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* This word is most frequently used in the plural / collective sense, as above.

